request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,70,2075,8,284,856,61,17,481,220,16,16,87,488,220,18,15,4779,323,1077,400,69,2075,15087,387,264,47311,1741,429,198,78045,70,955,2075,593,284,856,61,19,481,220,16,19,87,61,18,488,220,21,17,87,61,17,481,220,24,16,87,488,220,19,17,7110,60,9885,279,2629,315,678,3204,2750,315,400,69,7,16,15,47822,16,15,15,16630,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $g(x) = x^2 - 11x + 30,$ and let $f(x)$ be a polynomial such that\n\\[g(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42.\\]Find the sum of all possible values of $f(10^{100}).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"0972c0e98995acc74c63d8c3ca9dfa01a61cb8dd18ca31657f6114d89c5c423f"},"seconds":77.03101015090942,"seed":117852503961258445,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( f(10^{100}) \\) given that \\( g(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\) and \\( g(x) = x^2 - 11x + 30 \\), we start by considering the form of \\( f(x) \\). Since \\( g(f(x)) \\) is a quartic polynomial, \\( f(x) \\) must be a quadratic polynomial, because the composition of a quadratic polynomial with another quadratic polynomial results in a quartic polynomial.\n\nLet's assume \\( f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \\). Then,\n\\[ g(f(x)) = (ax^2 + bx + c)^2 - 11(ax^2 + bx + c) + 30. \\]\nWe need to match this to the given polynomial \\( x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\).\n\nFirst, expand \\( (ax^2 + bx + c)^2 \\):\n\\[ (ax^2 + bx + c)^2 = a^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2)x^2 + 2bcx + c^2. \\]\nThen,\n\\[ g(f(x)) = a^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2)x^2 + 2bcx + c^2 - 11(ax^2 + bx + c) + 30 \\]\n\\[ = a^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2 - 11a)x^2 + (2bc - 11b)x + (c^2 - 11c + 30). \\]\nBy comparing coefficients with \\( x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\), we get the following system of equations:\n1. \\( a^2 = 1 \\)\n2. \\( 2ab = -14 \\)\n3. \\( 2ac + b^2 - 11a = 62 \\)\n4. \\( 2bc - 11b = -91 \\)\n5. \\( c^2 - 11c + 30 = 42 \\)\n\nFrom the first equation, \\( a = 1 \\) or \\( a = -1 \\).\n\n**Case 1: \\( a = 1 \\)**\nThen \\( 2b = -14 \\) so \\( b = -7 \\).\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = -7 \\) into the third equation:\n\\[ 2c + 49 - 11 = 62 \\]\n\\[ 2c + 38 = 62 \\]\n\\[ 2c = 24 \\]\n\\[ c = 12. \\]\nCheck the fourth equation:\n\\[ 2(-7)(12) - 11(-7) = -168 + 77 = -91. \\]\nCheck the fifth equation:\n\\[ 12^2 - 11 \\cdot 12 + 30 = 144 - 132 + 30 = 42. \\]\nSo, \\( f(x) = x^2 - 7x + 12 \\) is a solution.\n\n**Case 2: \\( a = -1 \\)**\nThen \\( -2b = -14 \\) so \\( b = 7 \\).\nSubstitute \\( a = -1 \\) and \\( b = 7 \\) into the third equation:\n\\[ -2c + 49 + 11 = 62 \\]\n\\[ -2c + 60 = 62 \\]\n\\[ -2c = 2 \\]\n\\[ c = -1. \\]\nCheck the fourth equation:\n\\[ 2(7)(-1) - 11(7) = -14 - 77 = -91. \\]\nCheck the fifth equation:\n\\[ (-1)^2 - 11(-1) + 30 = 1 + 11 + 30 = 42. \\]\nSo, \\( f(x) = -x^2 + 7x - 1 \\) is a solution.\n\nThe possible values of \\( f(10^{100}) \\) are:\n1. \\( f(10^{100}) = (10^{100})^2 - 7 \\cdot 10^{100} + 12 = 10^{200} - 7 \\cdot 10^{100} + 12 \\)\n2. \\( f(10^{100}) = -(10^{100})^2 + 7 \\cdot 10^{100} - 1 = -10^{200} + 7 \\cdot 10^{100} - 1 \\)\n\nThe sum of all possible values is:\n\\[ (10^{200} - 7 \\cdot 10^{100} + 12) + (-10^{200} + 7 \\cdot 10^{100} - 1) = 11. \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all possible values of \\( f(10^{100}) \\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{11}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
